nemo_rl.patch = our changes to nemo_rl/ and examples/ (22 files), used by the paper's NeMo-RL runs (MaxRL on
Math12K from the base model, coding RL on KodCode):
  - MaxRL advantage estimator (grpo.adv_estimator.name=maxrl: A = (r - mean) / (mean + eps), baseline
    subtraction, optional ceiling / eps smoothing) next to upstream GRPO
  - math environment: verl boxed-answer reward (verl_math_reward), strict-form verifiers, and the sandboxed
    unit-test reward for coding (math_verify_impl=code_tests -> unified_training code reward)
  - async/checkpoint/dataloader hardening, system-interpreter actors (NEMO_RL_PY_EXECUTABLES_SYSTEM=1),
    logger options (log_data_jsonl, step_mult)
nemo_rl/data/ is NOT patched: the runs used upstream's nemo_rl/data unchanged.

Runtime of the paper's runs: one Python 3.13 venv with torch 2.10.0, vllm 0.17.1, transformers 4.57.6,
ray 2.57.0, accelerate 1.14.0, datasets 4.0.0, hydra-core 1.3.5, omegaconf 2.3.1, math-verify 0.8.0,
DTensor (FSDP) policy backend, sequence packing off.
requirements-nemo-rl.txt pins this runtime; scripts/setup_nemo_rl_env.sh builds it and runs setup.sh.

Verification (2026-10-27): applying the unscrubbed patch to a clean checkout of the commit above reproduces
the code the runs executed byte for byte (nemo_rl/, examples/; nemo_rl/data identical to upstream). The
shipped patch differs from that only in comments, one error-message string, two entries of an
environment-variable denylist (internal names removed) and three imports renamed to this repository's
package (unified_training.code_reward / checkpoint_milestones / strict_math_gate; the first two are
byte-identical to the modules the runs imported, the third is only reached by math_verify_impl=
hf_math_verify_strict, which no paper run used). Needs src/ of this repository on PYTHONPATH.
